Benefits Committee External Review Guidelines Policies Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Emergency Procedures Handbook Grievance Policy Title IX & Misconduct Policy Human Resources Employment Opportunities Benefits Employee Resources Policies SUPPORTING OUR MISSION AND VALUES Your Guide to Working at Whitman Whitman College’s Human Resources department is dedicated to supporting the college’s mission and values by attracting, developing, and retaining a diverse and talented workforce. Whether you are looking for information on employment opportunities, benefits and compensation, professional development or support services, our team is here to help. Benefits Employment Opportunities Employee Resources Policies Are you or a dependant struggling with mental health? Reach out to one of our mental health resources available to you and your dependents. Mental Health Resources Whitman By The Numbers 327 Staff (Full Time & Part Time) 204 Faculty (Full Time & Part Time) 19.6% Staff of Color (Full Time) 21% Faculty of Color (Full Time) Have questions related to Human Resources? Get answers and guidance from our HR experts here! Email us at hr@whitman.edu . Learn More Human Resources Staff Erika Cerda Associate Vice President for Human Resources Cara Setchell Associate Director of Human Resources Atarah Pinder Assistant Director for Faculty Human Resources Kate Brodland Senior Human Resources Generalist Carol Allen Senior Human Resources Generalist More Information & Resources Prospective Employee Resources Faculty Employment Opportunities Staff Employment Opportunities Applicants Benefits Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Current Employee Resources Staff Handbook Benefits Policies Forms Performance Appraisal myWhitman Washington Paid Family and Medical Leave: English Spanish Student Employee Resources Career and Community Engagement Center Office Information Memorial Building 104-107 345 Boyer Ave. Walla Walla, WA 99362 Office hours: Monday - Friday 8 a.m. - Noon; 1:00 p