ent Employment Welty Health and Counseling Center Quick Links Bon Appetit Bookstore Campus Map Career Resources Communications Conferences & Events Getting to Whitman College Giving Human Resources Institutional Research Job Opportunities Penrose Library Security Technology Services Welty Health & Counseling Center WhitLife Whitman Stories Apply Visit Whitman Alumni Make a Gift Stories Events Fellowships and Grants Career Prep Career Prep Fellowships and Grants On Becoming a Fellowship Candidate Fellowships and Grants Requiring Nomination Beinecke Scholarship Fulbright U.S. Student Program Gaither Junior Fellows Program Goldwater Scholarship Marshall Scholarship Projects for Peace Rhodes Scholarship Truman Scholarship Udall Scholarship Watson Fellowship Fellowships and Grants by Class Year Opportunities for Alumni Opportunities for Seniors Opportunities for Juniors Opportunities for Sophomores Opportunities for First-Year Students Contact Fellowships and Grants On Becoming a Fellowship Candidate Fellowships and Grants Requiring Nomination Fellowships and Grants by Class Year Contact Make Meaningful Contributions Unlock Your True Potential The Fellowships and Grants team at the Career and Community Engagement Center provides support to students and alumni in their application for nationally and globally competitive grants, fellowships and scholarships. Through these awards, Whitties can foster self-reflection and expand their understanding of different issues, ideas, and values—and themselves. Our goal is to help individuals develop critical thinking skills so they can increase the value that they bring to their communities. Explore Opportunities by Class Year Contact the F&G Team Since the year 2000, over 650 Whitman students and alumni have earned distinguished fellowships and grants, including: 32 Watson Fellowships 112 Fulbright U.S. Student Program Awards 64 Gilman International Scholarships 11 Udall Scholarships 47 National Science Foundation Graduate Research Fellowships 13 Goldwater Scholarships I went to an information session, talked to Fellowships and Grants about it and I took home a Watson Fellowship pamphlet and pinned it to my corkboard for the next four years. I knew it was something I wanted to strive for, but I never thought it was going to happen, to be honest. Liam Voorhees '21 , Environmental Humanities Major Find upcoming info sessions & drop-in hours on our calendar Find upcoming info sessions & drop-in hours on our calendar The Keys to Success How to Become a Fellowship Candidate Are you looking for help with a competitive fellowship application? Look no further! Our resources will cover everything you need to know to stand out as a candidate. Our Fellowships and Grants Team can provide support throughout your journey as well as connect you with mentors who have been in similar positions before. With the right knowledge and dedication to personal growth and development, your chances of success increase significantly. Become a Fellowship Candidate Become a Fellowship Candidate News and Features More News and Features Whitties Earned Dozens of Noteworthy Fellowships & Grants This Year July 17, 2026 Riley Cooper ’26: Storyteller, Filmmaker & Animal Advocate June 29, 2026 Maryanne Ndung’u ’26: Empowering Entrepreneurship Around the World June 29, 2026 More News and Features 345 Boyer Ave. Walla Walla, WA 99362 General: 509-527-5111 Admission: 509-527-5176 Apply Visit Request Info Bias Reporting Grievance Policy Nondiscrimination Policy Right to Know Title IX & Sexual Misconduct Disability and Accessibility Privacy Policy Whitman Online Terms of Service © 2025 Whitman College. All Rights Reserved."
