ment Whitties Helping Whitties Career Prep Real-World Experience Through the Whitman Internship Grant Life at Whitman Clubs and Activities Community Engagement Dining at Whitman Harper Joy Theatre International Student & Scholar Services New Student Orientation Outdoor Program Pathways Leadership Program Reid Campus Center Residence Halls Residence Life Sorority & Fraternity Life Student Activities Student Employment Welty Health and Counseling Center Search About Accessibility at Whitman Campus Map Contact Us Getting to Whitman College Inclusive Excellence Land Acknowledgment Native American Outreach Our Community President & Leadership Rankings and What Really Matters Strategic Planning Sustainability Whitman Magazine Academics Academic Calendar Catalog Center for Global Studies Community Outreach Fellowships and Grants First Year Seminars Global Whitman Graduation Requirements International Student & Scholar Services Majors & Programs Penrose Library Registrar Research at Whitman STEM Hub Study Abroad Whitman’s Faculty Admission & Aid Apply Early Decision Applying to Whitman Class of 2030 & Transfer Students Clubs and Activities Connect With Us Early Financial Aid Guarantee Financial Aid & Costs Getting to Whitman College Learn More About Whitman Request Information The Perfect College Town The Whitman 10% Promise Transfer Students Visit Whitman Whitman on the Road Why Whitman? Athletics Athletic Facility Hours Athletics Club Sports Intramural Sports Resources and Rules Varsity Athletics W Club Career Prep Career and Community Engagement Center Career Coaching Community Engagement Fellowships and Grants Internships Student Employment Whitties Helping Whitties Life at Whitman Clubs and Activities Community Engagement Dining at Whitman Harper Joy Theatre International Student & Scholar Services New Student Orientation Outdoor Program Pathways Leadership Program Reid Campus Center Residence Halls Residence Life Sorority & Fraternity Life Student Activities Student Employment Welty Health and Counseling Center Quick Links Bon Appetit Bookstore Campus Map Career Resources Communications Conferences & Events Getting to Whitman College Giving Human Resources Institutional Research Job Opportunities Penrose Library Security Technology Services Welty Health & Counseling Center WhitLife Whitman Stories Apply Visit Whitman Alumni Make a Gift Stories Events Academics Academics Whitman’s Faculty As a Whitman student, you’ll be inspired by the depth of knowledge, the breadth of interests, and the scholarly and creative achievements of the professors. Dedicated teachers . Our full-time faculty comprises 175 dynamic and experienced professors. While many of them have earned national recognition for their scholarship, what truly sets them apart is their passion for teaching and mentoring their students. A 9-to-1 student-faculty ratio, an average class size of 17, and the fact that most Whitman faculty live in neighborhoods close to campus mean that as a Whitman student, you’ll develop deep and productive intellectual and professional relationships with your professors. You’ll interact closely with them in the classroom. Work with them on real-world research projects. Accompany them on exciting study-abroad trips around the world. You’ll also run into them on and off campus at events. Renowned scholars . They are accessible, supportive and involved. They are dedicated mentors. But as a student here, you’ll quickly discover that Whitman professors are also uncompromising when it comes to academic rigor. They create an environment that encourages you to ask questions, to take intellectual risks, to pursue new insights and make new connections, often across disciplines. But they also demand 100 percent commitment and dedication to scholarship of the highest quality—both from their students as well as from themselves. This is one reason why they also continue to develop their own research, professional, and pedagogical skills through the discussions, lectures, workshops, and seminars organized at Whitman’s Center for Teaching and Learning . Professional honors . Not surprisingly, Whitman faculty regularly receive grants and fellowships from a variety of prestigious national and regional organizations, including: Battelle Research Institute Fulbright Fellows Program Howard Hughes Medical Institute Luce Foundation National Endowment for the Arts National Endowment for the Humanities National Institutes of Health National Science Foundation PEW Charitable Trust William and Flora Hewlett Foundation Academics Majors & Programs General Studies First Year Seminars Learning Outcomes Academic Calendar Convocation Convocation 2026 Convocation 2025 Convocation 2024 Convocation 2023 Final Exam Schedule Commencement Graduating Seniors Senior Degree Checklist Schedule of Events Baccalaureate Guest Accessibility Frequently Asked Questions Extreme Weather Plan Commencement History 2026 Commencement 2025 Commencement 2024 Commencement 2023 Commencement Honorary Degrees Commencement Map Catalog Graduation Requirements Whitman’s Faculty Faculty & Staff Emeriti Study Abroad Penrose Library Fellowships and Grants Honor Societies Phi Beta Kappa Standards for Election New Members German Honor Society Research at Whitman Whitman Undergraduate Conference Past Events 2025 Whitman Undergraduate Conference 2024 Whitman Undergraduate Conference 2023 Whitman Undergraduate Conference 2022 Whitman Undergraduate Conference Fred Hutch Cancer Center Summer Research 2011 Summer Research Interns 2010 Summer Research Interns 2009 Summer Research Interns Mayo SURF Program Global Whitman Immersive Learning at Whitman Integrated Advising at Whitman STEM Hub STEM Stories Resources Opportunities The Center for Writing and Speaking COWS Staff Courses in Writing and Speaking Disability Access Services Accommodate Portal Getting Started Academic Accommodations Testing Center Dietary Accommodations Housing Accommodations Emotional Support Animals Docum