nt Whitties Helping Whitties Career Prep Real-World Experience Through the Whitman Internship Grant Life at Whitman Clubs and Activities Community Engagement Dining at Whitman Harper Joy Theatre International Student & Scholar Services New Student Orientation Outdoor Program Pathways Leadership Program Reid Campus Center Residence Halls Residence Life Sorority & Fraternity Life Student Activities Student Employment Welty Health and Counseling Center Search About Accessibility at Whitman Campus Map Contact Us Getting to Whitman College Inclusive Excellence Land Acknowledgment Native American Outreach Our Community President & Leadership Rankings and What Really Matters Strategic Planning Sustainability Whitman Magazine Academics Academic Calendar Catalog Center for Global Studies Community Outreach Fellowships and Grants First Year Seminars Global Whitman Graduation Requirements International Student & Scholar Services Majors & Programs Penrose Library Registrar Research at Whitman STEM Hub Study Abroad Whitman’s Faculty Admission & Aid Apply Early Decision Applying to Whitman Class of 2030 & Transfer Students Clubs and Activities Connect With Us Early Financial Aid Guarantee Financial Aid & Costs Getting to Whitman College Learn More About Whitman Request Information The Perfect College Town The Whitman 10% Promise Transfer Students Visit Whitman Whitman on the Road Why Whitman? Athletics Athletic Facility Hours Athletics Club Sports Intramural Sports Resources and Rules Varsity Athletics W Club Career Prep Career and Community Engagement Center Career Coaching Community Engagement Fellowships and Grants Internships Student Employment Whitties Helping Whitties Life at Whitman Clubs and Activities Community Engagement Dining at Whitman Harper Joy Theatre International Student & Scholar Services New Student Orientation Outdoor Program Pathways Leadership Program Reid Campus Center Residence Halls Residence Life Sorority & Fraternity Life Student Activities Student Employment Welty Health and Counseling Center Quick Links Bon Appetit Bookstore Campus Map Career Resources Communications Conferences & Events Getting to Whitman College Giving Human Resources Institutional Research Job Opportunities Penrose Library Security Technology Services Welty Health & Counseling Center WhitLife Whitman Stories Apply Visit Whitman Alumni Make a Gift Stories Events Career Coaching Services and Programs Career Prep Career and Community Engagement Center Career Development Services and Programs Career and Community Engagement Center Our Staff Career Coaching Career Development Resources for Job Seekers Career Exploration & Major Pathways Industry-Specific Job Boards Interviews Networking Resume, CVs and Cover Letters Resumes Cover Letters CVs Salary Negotiation Services and Programs Career Coaching Student Career Advisors Craft Your Future Whitties Helping Whitties Internships Parker Dewey Micro-Internships Whitman Internship Grant (WIG) Student Internship Stories On-Campus Student Employment Next Steps for Seniors Community Engagement CE Volunteer Programs Build a Volunteer Opportunity Community Fellow Program Community Fellow Blog CE on Involve Ben Rabinowitz Award Fellowships and Grants Graduate and Professional School For International Students Recruit at Whitman College Recruitment Policies and Practices Guide to Hiring International Students WIG Information for Employers Information for Internship Supervisors Handshake Open On-Campus Student Jobs Summer in Seattle Career and Community Engagement Center Our Staff Career Coaching Career Development Community Engagement Fellowships and Grants Graduate and Professional School For International Students Recruit at Whitman College Handshake Open On-Campus Student Jobs Summer in Seattle Your Future, Your Path Personalized Support Every Step of the Way Even before you arrive at Whitman, you’ll connect with your dedicated career coach. Over the next four years, you’ll work together to create a clear roadmap that supports your growth and development as you consider what professional passions and career paths speak to you. And by the time you graduate, you'll have the skills, confidence and connections for whatever comes next, whether it's going to grad school, pursuing an international fellowship or launching into your first career. How Career Coaching Works Career coaching at Whitman is a four-year journey that grows with you. From your first year through graduation, your coach will help you take meaningful steps—from discovering your strengths to building experience and connecting with mentors—so you’re always moving forward with purpose. Your coach will guide you through a process with four key practices designed to help you grow with confidence and gain the clarity, skills and connections needed to shape a meaningful future. Self-Discovery Exploration Reflection Action Self-Discovery Understand your strengths, interests and values, and how they align with a variety of career fields. Exploration Access on-campus, community, and professional opportunities that allow you to gain skills, networks, and insights about potential career paths that interest you. Reflection Connect the dots between your learning, experiences and plans for the future. Action Take steps to move toward your professional goals and aspirations. Meet the Coaches Our career coaches are thoughtful guides, great listeners, and enthusiastic champions of your growth. They’ll get to know you, cheer you on, and help you navigate every step of your professional journey with confidence.  Current students can find their coach's name by accessing their profile through MyWhitman . Kimberly Rolfe Phil Marr Victoria Wolff Nadine Stecklein Marisol Becerra Cat Diebel-Wilson Caitlin Kiesz Lindsay Szramek Kimberly Rolfe (she/her/hers) Director of the Career and Community Engagement Center | Career Coach As Director of the Career and Community Engagement Center, I oversee operations, staff and resources to ensure that students can connect to the people and experiences that will help to shape their futures. We are a mighty team with a diverse set of experiences and identities, working together to open relevant and exciting opportunities for student learning outside of the classroom. I joined the Center in 2013 after spending 20-ish years in a variety of sales, marketing, and management roles in the apparel industry. Having the opportunity to now utilize what I learned over the course of my career as the Center creates a holistic and relevant set of programs and tools to connect students to our community and their life beyond Whitman has been an incredibly rewarding experience. Schedule an Appointment Drop-In Hours Phil Marr (he/him/his) Director for Employer Engagement | Career Coach As Director for Employer Engagement, I'm focused on building the employer and alumni partnerships that expand what Whitman students see as possible — connecting them to internships, careers and professional relationships that shape their paths long after graduation. I came to this role with more than a decade of experience working at the intersection of industry and education. At McKinstry, one of the Pacific Northwest's largest built environment companies, I developed and managed corporate education partnerships — working from inside an organization to understand what meaningful collaboration between employers and institutions actually requires. At Degrees of Change, I served as Senior Director of Career Pathways, directing the Strickland Fellowship, a career pathways fellowship bridging higher education, students and industry partners. Earlier in my career I worked at Communities in Schools of Washington and UW Tacoma, in roles that grounded me in youth development and community partnership and shaped how I think about what employer partnerships can do to help students prepare to step into a new professional environment. At Whitman, that thread continues. My goal is to build partnerships that showcase the value of Whitman students and expand access to the immersive learning experiences that elevate a Whitman education — including Summer in Seattle , our cohort program connecting students to one of the country's most dynamic job markets. Schedule an Appointment Drop-In Hours Victoria Wolff '12 (she/her/hers) Director for Career Development | Career Coach With over 15 years of experience in higher education, I have focused on advancing student learning, career development, and equitable access to opportunity. At Whitman's Career and Community Engagement Center, I lead Career Development efforts and supervise a team of professionals. Together, we design and deliver impactful coaching and programming to prepare students and alumni for meaningful post-graduate paths. I oversee a broad portfolio, including career coaching, employer engagement, career education, and student-alumni mentoring, while providing strategic direction and leading cross-functional initiatives. I'm especially proud of the collaborative environment we've built, where we co-create workshops, integrate career education into academics, and use data to drive alignment with institutional goals. Building relationships across campus and in the community is central to my leadership approach. Originally from Berlin, Germany, I earned my B.A. in English, History, and Education from Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin and later completed an M.Ed. focused on English and History. Fun fact: I first came to Whitman in 2010-11 as a visiting instructor in the German Studies program and lived in Das Deutsche Haus . Schedule an Appointment Drop-In Hours Nadine Stecklein (she/her/ella) Associate Director for Employer Engagement and Internship Programs | Career Coach I joined the Career and Community Engagement Center in 2022 after spending a decade working in the public sector and supporting student success in higher education institutions throughout Southern California. I am a proud first-generation, working-class graduate of Whittier College (go Poets!) and earned my Master's in Public Administration with an emphasis in nonprofit management. I am a huge believer in experiential learning and love helping students explore opportunities such as internships, research, community engagement, and other hands-on experiences. My own undergraduate internships played a significant role in helping me discover what I was passionate about and what wasn't the right fit. Those experiences continue to shape how I work with and support students as they navigate their own journeys. Originally from Los Angeles, I moved to Walla Walla in 2018 and quickly became involved in the community. In addition to my role at Whitman, I serve on the College Place City Council, participate in the College Place Lions Club, and volunteer with the Blue Mountain Humane Society. Outside of work, you will usually find me listening to an audiobook, attending one of my many book clubs (I'm currently a member of nine!), or spending time in the community. I am also always up for boba tea or a spicy chai. In my opinion, The Patisserie serves the best spicy chai in town! Schedule an Appointment Drop-In Hours Marisol Becerra (she/her/hers) Programs and Budget Coordinator | Career Coach As the Programs and Budget Coordinator for Whitman College’s Career and Community Engagement Center, I support the Center’s programs, operations, and financial management while helping to create a welcoming and supportive experience for students, campus partners, and community members. My work includes managing program budgets and internship endowments, coordinating financial processes, supervising student administrative staff, and supporting the implementation of programs and events across the Center. I also oversee Whitman’s America Reads/America Counts (ARAC) Immersive Learning Program, working closely with ARAC Leaders and local school partners to coordinate placements, schedules, communication, and overall program operations. This role allows me to combine student development, community engagement, and program management in a meaningful way. I have been part of the Whitman community since 2012 and have grown into a role that allows me to combine my strengths in organization, relationship building, student support, and program administration. I also bring an entrepreneurial perspective to my work and enjoy finding practical ways to improve systems, strengthen programs, and support the people around me. Having grown up in the Walla Walla Valley, I value staying connected to the local community and contributing whenever I can. Outside of work, I enjoy spending time with my family, camping, and planning gatherings with my extended family. I also love amusement parks and anything that gets my adrenaline going: the higher, faster, and more thrilling the roller coaster, the better! Schedule an Appointment Cat Diebel-Wilson (they/them) Career Development and Fellowships Specialist | Career Coach As a Career Development and Fellowships Specialist, I coach students through the career exploration and planning process and help students and alumni think through graduate school plans and produce compelling materials for admissions and funding applications alike. I'm a graduate of the Classics program at the University of Kansas (M.A. '08) and the University of Missouri-Kansas City (B.A. '05), and also spent some years in the Classics Ph.D. program at the University of British Columbia, leaving ABD (all but dissertation). I came to Whitman from the University of Colorado Boulder, where I worked with graduate students to help them realize their academic and professional goals. In my free time I read (mostly fantasy and science fiction), watch documentaries (mostly cold case/true crime), write, and paint, accompanied (and sometimes hindered) by my dachshund, Mulder and my cat, Pram. Schedule an Appointment Drop-In Hours Caitlin Kiesz (she/her/hers) Career Development Specialist | Career Coach Just like many college students, I was uncertain how my professional journey would progress after graduating with my B.A. in Sociology. Ultimately, my path developed as I tried out new opportunities. Exploring different options helped uncover my passion for working with students as they evaluate their emerging interests and assess possible careers. My experiences as a Resident Advisor in college, working for a local bank, attaining my M.Ed. in College Student Services Administration, and filling a few different roles at Whitman College have all taught me the importance and benefit of building connections, trying new activities, and regular reflection on one's interests (and disinterests!), values, and skill sets. As a Career Development Specialist and Career Coach, I am excited to team up with Whitties as they continue on their own unique journeys. I provide all students with career-focused support and specialize in assisting students pursuing a social science degree. I am also the Career Coach for all Garrett-Sherwood Scholars. Outside of work, I enjoy spending time with my husband Cory, my son Leland, our two shelties, Theo and Isla, and our two cats, Andi and Jasper. I grew up in Olympia, Washington, and have a fondness for rainy days and coffee! My favorite season is autumn (beautiful colors, sweater weather, and college football - Go Cougs, Go Beavs, Go Blue!). Over the summer, my home away from home is Northport, Michigan, on the shore of Lake Michigan. I look forward to getting to know you! Schedule an Appointment Drop-In Hours Lindsay Szramek (she/her/hers) Career Development Specialist in STEM | Career Coach I was brought into the Career and Community Engagement Center in 2021 as a point person for students exploring STEM careers. My background is in the geosciences, and I have taught at a number of institutions of higher learning, including Whitman. I always enjoy interacting with students and helping them think about what comes after college. In my current work, I develop a variety of interactive programs and work directly with students, both STEM and non-STEM, to help make the transition to life after Whitman easier. While I grew up in Oregon, I left for college and spent 20+ years outside the PNW in Maine, Alaska, Texas, Wisconsin, and Tennessee. My dogs and I are excited to be back so they can get more treats and visits from their grandparents. When not at work or obeying three bossy dogs, I like to spend time outside, collect rocks, collect fabric, and sew things. So if you are curious about what you could do in STEM or just want to talk about rocks, feel free to contact me! Schedule an Appointment Drop-In Hours More Than a Degree Get Ready to Make a Real Impact With personalized coaching, you can align your passions and experiences at Whitman with practical career preparation so you don’t have to choose between purpose and success. Your career coach will help you connect your values to real-world opportunities like internships, research, and community engagement. Career Development Community Engagement Internship Stories Fellowships and Grants First Jobs “Use all the resources that Whitman provides. Career coaching is very helpful and if you start early with planning your post-graduation plans, you can get very far and be well prepared for the transition.” Fabian G. ’25, Computer Science Major After his junior year, Fabian had a paid internship with Microsoft. Following that experience, he secured a full-time role with Microsoft as a Software Engineer. Career Success Starts Here Meet talented Whitties who, with the help of caring coaches and mentors, are making the most of their education and hands-on experiences. Not all paths are the same, but at Whitman, having dedicated assistance with career development and post-graduate planning helps students launch bright futures and successful careers. More Stories Bill Neff ’67 & Rita Neff ’69 Provide Challenge Gift for Endowment To Expand Immersive Learning With their lead gift, Trustee Emeritus Bill "
    },
