loyment Whitties Helping Whitties Career Prep Real-World Experience Through the Whitman Internship Grant Life at Whitman Clubs and Activities Community Engagement Dining at Whitman Harper Joy Theatre International Student & Scholar Services New Student Orientation Outdoor Program Pathways Leadership Program Reid Campus Center Residence Halls Residence Life Sorority & Fraternity Life Student Activities Student Employment Welty Health and Counseling Center Search About Accessibility at Whitman Campus Map Contact Us Getting to Whitman College Inclusive Excellence Land Acknowledgment Native American Outreach Our Community President & Leadership Rankings and What Really Matters Strategic Planning Sustainability Whitman Magazine Academics Academic Calendar Catalog Center for Global Studies Community Outreach Fellowships and Grants First Year Seminars Global Whitman Graduation Requirements International Student & Scholar Services Majors & Programs Penrose Library Registrar Research at Whitman STEM Hub Study Abroad Whitman’s Faculty Admission & Aid Apply Early Decision Applying to Whitman Class of 2030 & Transfer Students Clubs and Activities Connect With Us Early Financial Aid Guarantee Financial Aid & Costs Getting to Whitman College Learn More About Whitman Request Information The Perfect College Town The Whitman 10% Promise Transfer Students Visit Whitman Whitman on the Road Why Whitman? Athletics Athletic Facility Hours Athletics Club Sports Intramural Sports Resources and Rules Varsity Athletics W Club Career Prep Career and Community Engagement Center Career Coaching Community Engagement Fellowships and Grants Internships Student Employment Whitties Helping Whitties Life at Whitman Clubs and Activities Community Engagement Dining at Whitman Harper Joy Theatre International Student & Scholar Services New Student Orientation Outdoor Program Pathways Leadership Program Reid Campus Center Residence Halls Residence Life Sorority & Fraternity Life Student Activities Student Employment Welty Health and Counseling Center Quick Links Bon Appetit Bookstore Campus Map Career Resources Communications Conferences & Events Getting to Whitman College Giving Human Resources Institutional Research Job Opportunities Penrose Library Security Technology Services Welty Health & Counseling Center WhitLife Whitman Stories Apply Visit Whitman Alumni Make a Gift Stories Events Career and Community Engagement Center Career Prep Career and Community Engagement Center Community Engagement Our Mission We strive to build strong, sustainable relationships with community partners to create opportunities for students to come alongside members of the Walla Walla community through volunteer and fellowship experiences to support projects and initiatives identified by our partners as positively contributing to the community and their organizations’ purposes. If you're considering volunteering, remember these 5 “Best Practices for Volunteering” Keep Your Commitment. Carefully consider any volunteer opportunity and ensure that you are able to fully commit to the entirety of the project. Everyone has a lot to juggle so honor your personal capacity. Organizations will appreciate even a few hours of volunteering toward a larger project. Be a Good Representative . Remember that you are not only representing yourself, but also Whitman College. Ensure that you are doing so in a positive light. Learn the Why . Take the time to learn about the organization you will be volunteering with and ensure that you understand why the project is important. What is the impact of the project? Remember the Circumstances . Take time to understand circumstances of various times of the year/season/volunteering cycle and how they impact the organization’s ability to support the community. Make the Connection . You have the power to make a difference. Utilize your special skills, knowledge, and talents for good through volunteering. Take time to reflect on this experience and how it fits into your story, your experience as a Whittie, and your future endeavors. Don’t forget the folks in the CCEC are here to help you with your next steps. Reach out today! Don’t forget to share your experiences, photos and thoughts with the CCEC, we love seeing Whitties making an impact! We Have Many Community Engagement Programs! If you want to get involved with the greater Walla Walla and Whitman College communities, we have myriad programs open to volunteers. Our Community Engagement Programming allows Whitties to connect to the Walla Walla Community on a regular basis. In the News New Mural Highlights Latine Visibility Whitman Journey: Adam Simon ’26 Sharing a Story and Smile Through Volunteering Get to Know My Favorite Place on Earth Through Volunteering Whitman Students Help Feed the Valley by Gleaning Empowering Youth Through English Tri-College Community Day Connects Walla Walla’s Colleges Through Service Volunteers Hone Read-Aloud Techniques with the Walla Walla County Rural Library District Checking in With Newman Civic Fellow Adam Simon ’26 School’s Back in Session: Whitman Students Volunteer in WWPS Whitman College, local nonprofits partner to enrich community Outside the “Whitman Bubble”: Sharpstein Beautification Day Community Volunteer Fair: Helping Others and Helping You Whitman Students Build Skills and Connections as Community Fellows Whitman Pairs Community Engagement With Education Through Volunteering Our Whitman, My Story: Cassidy Washburn Community Fellows Build Skills & Connections Community Engagement by the numbers! Giving to Community Engagement If you believe in our mission and would like to help support our programs, you can give a gift using Whitman's online gift form. Career and Community Engagement Center Our Staff Career Coaching Career Development Resources for Job Seekers Career Exploration & Major Pathways Industry-Specific Job Boards Interviews Networking Resume, CVs and Cover Letters Resumes Cover Letters CVs Salary Negotiation Service