      "title": "Internships",
      "description": "Internships | Whitman College Skip to Content Apply Visit Whitman Alumni Make a Gift Stories Events Bon Appetit Bookstore Campus Map Career Resources Communications Conferences & Events Getting to Whitman College Giving Human Resources Institutional Research Job Opportunities Penrose Library Security Technology Services Welty Health & Counseling Center WhitLife Whitman Stories Alumni CARE Team Families Diversity & Inclusion President & Leadership Directories Alumni Directory myWhitman Search About Accessibility at Whitman Campus Map Contact Us Getting to Whitman College Inclusive Excellence Land Acknowledgment Native American Outreach Our Community President & Leadership Rankings and What Really Matters Strategic Planning Sustainability Whitman Magazine About Find out about Whitman's commitment to sustainability. Academics Academic Calendar Catalog Center for Global Studies Community Outreach Fellowships and Grants First Year Seminars Global Whitman Graduation Requirements International Student & Scholar Services Majors & Programs Penrose Library Registrar Research at Whitman STEM Hub Study Abroad Whitman’s Faculty Academics Learn how to pursue a fellowship, scholarship or grant opportunity. Admission & Aid Apply Early Decision Applying to Whitman Class of 2030 & Transfer Students Clubs and Activities Connect With Us Early Financial Aid Guarantee Financial Aid & Costs Getting to Whitman College Learn More About Whitman Request Information The Perfect College Town The Whitman 10% Promise Transfer Students Visit Whitman Whitman on the Road Why Whitman? Admission & Aid Join us on campus to experience the Whitman community in action! Athletics Athletic Facility Hours Athletics Club Sports Intramural Sports Resources and Rules Varsity Athletics W Club Athletics See when Whitman’s teams are playing this fall. Career Prep Career and Community Engagement Center Career Coaching Community Engagement Fellowships and Grants Internships Student Employment Whitties Helping Whitties Career Prep Real-World Experience Through the Whitman Internship Grant Life at Whitman Clubs and Activities Community Engagement Dining at Whitman Harper Joy Theatre International Student & Scholar Services New Student Orientation Outdoor Program Pathways Leadership Program Reid Campus Center Residence Halls Residence Life Sorority & Fraternity Life Student Activities Student Employment Welty Health and Counseling Center Search About Accessibility at Whitman Campus Map Contact Us Getting to Whitman College Inclusive Excellence Land Acknowledgment Native American Outreach Our Community President & Leadership Rankings and What Really Matters Strategic Planning Sustainability Whitman Magazine Academics Academic Calendar Catalog Center for Global Studies Community Outreach Fellowships and Grants First Year Seminars Global Whitman Graduation Requirements International Student & Scholar Services Majors & Programs Penrose Library Registrar Research at Whitman STEM Hub Study Abroad Whitman’s Faculty Admission & Aid Apply Early Decision Applying to Whitman Class of 2030 & Transfer Students Clubs and Activities Connect With Us Early Financial Aid Guarantee Financial Aid & Costs Getting to Whitman College Learn More About Whitman Request Information The Perfect College Town The Whitman 10% Promise Transfer Students Visit Whitman Whitman on the Road Why Whitman? Athletics Athletic Facility Hours Athletics Club Sports Intramural Sports Resources and Rules Varsity Athletics W Club Career Prep Career and Community Engagement Center Career Coaching Community Engagement Fellowships and Grants Internships Student Employment Whitties Helping Whitties Life at Whitman Clubs and Activities Community Engagement Dining at Whitman Harper Joy Theatre International Student & Scholar Services New Student Orientation Outdoor Program Pathways Leadership Program Reid Campus Center Residence Halls Residence Life Sorority & Fraternity Life Student Activities Student Employment Welty Health and Counseling Center Quick Links Bon Appetit Bookstore Campus Map Career Resources Communications Conferences & Events Getting to Whitman College Giving Human Resources Institutional Research Job Opportunities Penrose Library Security Technology Services Welty Health & Counseling Center WhitLife Whitman Stories Apply Visit Whitman Alumni Make a Gift Stories Events Career Development Career Prep Career and Community Engagement Center Career Development Internships Rachel Haughton '24 with Beaver Coalition in Asotin, WA Devon Player ‘23 with the Freedom Project in Renton, WA Shahrom Dehoti '24 with Harvust in Walla Walla, WA Riley Kraft ’23 with the Zelikowsky Lab in Salt Lake City, UT Alex Muller ’23 with Think Wild in Bend, OR What is an internship? Internships are opportunities for active learning outside of the classroom that allow students to bring their academic knowledge and theory to bear in real-world situations and professional settings.  Interns not only develop valuable practical skills but also build crucial connections with professionals in industries and areas they may wish to further pursue.  An internship can be a good way for a student to explore a new field before committing to a career pathway.  Employers value the opportunity to offer internships as a unique way to mentor and access potential talent, fostering a dynamic exchange of ideas and exertise. The National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) defines an internship as \"a form of experiential learning that integrates knowledge and theory learned in the classroom with practical application and skills development in a professional workplace setting.\"  Whitman students often participate in multiple internships over the course of their studies, each connected with one or more of their academic interests. How can an internship help me? By participating in an internship you can: Explore an industry, career path, or organization Gain practical, hands-on professional work experience Build and hone skills that employers look for when hiring college graduates Network with professionals and make valuable connections for references, future opportunties, and mentorship Apply knowledge acquired in the classroom to the outside workplace Where can I find internship opportunities? Whether you have an organization already in mind or aren't sure where to start, there are many resources available to assist in identifying an internship that is right for you. Browse both paid and unpaid internships posted on Handshake .  If you find an unpaid internship, you can apply for the Whitman Internship Grant . Sign up for Whitman's internship listserv: Whitman students should visit groups.google.com , search for \"internship alerts,\" and click the icon to join the group.  The listserv provides a monthly email that lists paid internship opportunities in various sectors. Consider the opportunities posted on Whitman's Parker-Dewey Micro-Internships page. Visit the careers or jobs webpages for employers you are curious about; locate additional employers through industry-specific job boards . Follow employers on LinkedIn and investigate their content while making sure that your own profile is up-to-date. Engage with employers' social media accounts. Utilize the Washington State Workforce Portal . Attend job and career fairs. Connect with your personal network to let them know that you are seeking an internship. What is the Whitman Internship Grant (WIG)? The Whitman Internship Grant is a competitive grant that can provide funding for students who secure or build an unpaid internship opportunity at nonprofit organizations, some for-profit organizations, and government offices either during a semester or over the summer.  Reach out to Associate Director for Employer Engagement and Internship Programs, Nadine Stecklein , with questions regarding the Whitman Internship Grant. What are Parker Dewey Micro-Internships? Parker Dewey Micro-Internships provide students from all majors with the opportunity to execute professional assignments that allow them to build and demonstrate skills while exploring a variety of career paths. Employers may use micro-internships to improve the effectiveness of hiring efforts or to obtain immediate help on projects if they or their team are overloaded. Visit the Parker Dewey website for more information.  (NOTE: students must have a U.S. work authorization in order to partake in this program.) Can I get course credit for an internship? IDSC 125 is a one-credit academic course, approved by a student's major advisor and supervised by a member of the Career and Community Engagement Center, which connects formal off-campus student experiences in applied settings (e.g., internships) with their academic major. Can I get assistance with applying for internships? Students and recent alumni can schedule appointments with CCEC staff members via Handshake for resume and cover letter review as well as for assistance with developing, finding, or securing an internship. Assistant Director for Internship Programs, Nadine Stecklein , is available for appointment scheduling on Handshake. More internship search resources: Whitman students can take advantage of multiple resources during the process of an internship search, including access to instructional guides and an internship database, consultation with peer advisors, and connecting with Whitman alumni who have expressed an interest in helping out.  See below for more information. Handshake Handshake is a social-media style job and internship platform for undergraduates and young alumni. Activate your account to access a variety of resources including internship postings, events sponsored by employers and by the CCEC, and a Resource Library compiled by CCEC staff, including an article specifically geared toward finding internships and research opportunities .  Handshake is also the place to schedule appointments with professional CCEC staff or SCAs for resume review, cover letter help, assistance in identifying internship resources, consulting about the Whitman Internship Grant, or just to talk about your future plans - whether you have any in mind yet, or not! Whitman Internship Database The Whitman Internship Database is temporarily offline and will return shortly. The Whitman Internship Database contains information on years of past internships held by Whitman students.  You can search and filter by location, major, and keywords.  Some of these internships were eligible for the Whitman Internship Grant . Whitman Connect Whitman Connect is Whitman's proprietary database of alumni, searchable by location, industry, occupation, major, campus groups and activities, and more.  Through Whitman Connect, students can research and contact alumni who have volunteered to support students’ professional exploration and preparation in a variety of ways. Please note that this tool is a private environment for professional conversations between students and alumni.  A positive, professional demeanor and responsible conduct is expected.  Please do not allow others to access this resource with your login credentials or use the platform for soliciting anything beyond career mentorship or advice. Stories of Whittie Internship Experiences Whitman students know that learning doesn't just happen in the classroom. That's why so many students participate in internships during their time at Whitman. Catch up on what Whitman Internship Grant recipients are doing and learning in internships all over the globe! Career and Community Engagement Center Our Staff Career Coaching Career Development Resources for Job Seekers Career Exploration & Major Pathways Industry-Specific Job Boards Interviews Networking Resume, CVs and Cover Letters Resumes Cover Letters CVs Salary Negotiation Services and Programs Career Coaching Student Career Advisors Craft Your Future Whitties Helping Whitties Internships Parker Dewey Micro-Internships Whitman Internship 