tudent Employment Welty Health and Counseling Center Quick Links Bon Appetit Bookstore Campus Map Career Resources Communications Conferences & Events Getting to Whitman College Giving Human Resources Institutional Research Job Opportunities Penrose Library Security Technology Services Welty Health & Counseling Center WhitLife Whitman Stories Apply Visit Whitman Alumni Make a Gift Stories Events Career Development Career Prep Career and Community Engagement Center Career Development Resources for Job Seekers Whether you are searching for a summer job or internship, opportunities during the academic year, or your first full-time role post-graduation, the Career and Community Engagement Center (CCEC) is here to guide you every step of the way. This page covers a variety of tools and resources that will help you be successful in your job search: you can explore curated job boards, application guides, identity-based support and labor rights information below. Remember: you can meet with a Career Coach to develop a job search strategy, get feedback and make the most of the tools available to you. If you are a current student or recent grad, you can also access more career resources and tools in the Handshake Resource Library . The Job Search Toolkit Your quick access hub for every phase of you job application journey: Resumes, CVs & Cover Letters Finding Opportunities & Job Boards Networking & Connection Interviewing & Offer Negotiation Career Exploration & Pathways Build an ATS-friendly, high-impact resume or tailored cover letter. Use these application tips, materials and guides to help you stand out! Resume Guides CV Examples Cover Letter Writing Tips Connect directly with employers who are hiring Whitties like you! Handshake Platform Industry-Specific Job Boards Parker Dewey Micro-Internships On-Campus Employment Tap into the alumni network and build professional relationships. Whitties Helping Whitties Whitman Connect Whitman College LinkedIn LinkedIn Profile Guide Informational Interviewing and Networking Emails Prepare for behavioral questions and case interviews, and learn how to evaluate and negotiate job offers. STAR Interview Preparation Guide Interview Tips and Tools Salary Negotiation Strategies Not sure what’s next? Align your major with real-world career paths. What Can I Do With This Major? Career Pathfinder Next Steps for Seniors Inclusive & Identity-Focused Career Resources At Whitman, we recognize that identity plays a significant role in navigating the workplace, evaluating organizational culture, and deciding when or how to disclose personal information during a job search. Explore tailored job platforms, professional affinity networks and career guidance tailored to your unique background below. Resources for BIPOC Students & Religious Communities: Professional development associations, diverse talent networks, and guidance on identifying inclusive workplace cultures. Latine & Hispanic Communities Healthcare and Social Work National Hispanic Medical Association ** National Latinx Psychological Association ** American Society of Hispanic Psychiatry ** National Hispanic Pharmacists Association ** National Association of Puerto Rican and Hispanic Social Workers ** The National Hispanic Science Network ** Latinx Veterinary Medical Association ** Latino Social Work Coalition and Scholarship Fund Government and Law Congressional Hispanic Caucus Institute ** Congressional Hispanic Staff Association Hispanic National Bar Association ** DREAM Bar Association Latina Lawyers Bar Association ** League of United Latin American Citizens ** STEM and Business Green Latinos (Environmental Science Association) Society of Hispanic Professional Engineers ** Hispanic Association of Computer Scientists Society for the Advancement of Chicanos/Hispanics and Native Americans in Science National Society of Hispanic Physicists ** Latinas in STEM Techqueria: Latinos in Tech ** Association of Latino Professionals in Finance and Accounting